ok     a ring of 4096 holds 4095 bytes
ok     the byte that did not fit was counted, not lost silently
ok     the bytes came out in the order they went in
ok     an emptied ring has nothing pending
ok     ten bytes cross the end of the ring and come back in order
ok     a 68-byte line fits whole, and a reset keeps the drop total
ok     quoted newline stays uncommitted and EOF copies no NUL
ok     a full canonical line reserves its committing delimiter
ok     partial reads keep the delimiter and editing cannot cross it
ok     switching to raw removes EOF metadata without losing bytes
ok     BusyBox init sane settings are all accepted
ok     unsupported flags and timing fail without mutating settings
ok     ICRNL IXON ISIG and IEXTEN decode the real control characters
ok     IXOFF hysteresis requests stop at high water and releases at low water
ok     a full canonical line and its tab-width kill fit as compact echo operations
ok     an echo operation beyond capacity is counted and never blocks
